      sources: "Sources: Learn, Configure role settings in PIM; conditionalAccessApplications (v1.0 and beta). Chapter 04, “The checks.”",
      say: `Before anything is written, nine checks run. The first two are the two halves of the lockout: approval with no approver, and too few emergency accounts holding Global Administrator. Others keep approvers separate from the people they approve, keep every file inside its bounds, and refuse a wave until the earlier ones match. Any finding blocks the write. One check can't be automated: whether the activation gate's policy is on lives in a beta property, so a person has to state it, with a flag, after Chapter 3's run shows it's on.`,
      detail: `Before anything is written, Test-PaPimSetting and New-PaPimPlan report: PA-PIM-01 Finding, approval required with no approver (Learn: half of the documented lockout). PA-PIM-02 Finding, fewer emergency accounts with permanent, active, direct Global Administrator than emergency-access.json requires (Learn: the other half; Chapter 02). PA-PIM-03 Finding, an approver group that is also the role's eligible group (design guidance: Book 04, Chapter 08). PA-PIM-04 Finding, a file outside Learn's bounds or its tier's cap: activation, eligibility, permanent eligible, active assignments over 15 days, permanent active on any role but Global Administrator, missing approval or ticket (Learn's bounds; Appendix B's caps, design guidance; the owner's 15-day decision). PA-PIM-05 Warn, an authentication context: its Conditional Access policy must be On before the rule is set (Learn). PA-PIM-06 Finding, no policy for the role at tenant scope. PA-PIM-07 Finding, an earlier rollout wave that doesn't match its files yet (design guidance: the plan's order). PA-PIM-08 Warn, eligibility outside the role's PRV group (design guidance; the access review removes it, Chapter 07). PA-PIM-09 Warn and Info: a standing active assignment, a user to convert, or a service principal to document (Warn); an emergency account or a documented exception (Info) (Book 04, Chapter 08). Any Finding blocks -Apply. PA-PIM-05 can't be checked from v1.0: the Conditional Access policy's authentication context target is a beta property. So -Apply needs -ActivationGateChecked, a person's statement, made after Chapter 03's run shows no PA-CA-04 for PIM-Activation-c1, that the policy is On (research gaps, row 44). Chapter 06 asks the same of its Azure role settings.`,
